    "body": "Fact for #706 (UMA): while building #960 the worker found that `pick::roles::align_roles` in open PR #706 has its `(Role::Z, Role::Y)` arm copied from `(Y, X)`, so a Z pick + a Y pick puts Z on Y and the work offset lies on its back (posted moves turned 90°). #960 carries the one-hunk fix (`let y = square_to(g2, d2.dir, a, tilt)?; (cross(y, a), y, a)`) pinned by `set_wcs_from_features_lands_on_the_guis_frame_as_one_undo_step`. Not posted on #706 itself: that waits for the maintainer/owner. Main is unaffected while #706 is unmerged.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
